    {
      "@id": "chem:ActiveSite_0001",
      "@type": [
        "chebi:ChemicalEntity",
        "cpo:ActiveSite",
        "hlo:Fixed"
      ],
      "schema:name": "Platinum active site (H-type)",
      "dcterms:isPartOf": {
        "@id": "chem:Molecule_0002"
      },
      "schema:comment": "A distinguishable kind of site on the platinum catalyst surface (dcterms:isPartOf chem:Molecule_0002, which carries the matching dcterms:hasPart) that binds hydrogen atoms and the hydrogenation intermediates. Carrier of cpo:boundTo on the occupation states cat(H), cat-H, cat-RYE, cat-RYA, cat-REA and cat-RDEt; the reaction library placeholder placeholder:CatalystSiteH resolves to this entry. Kept as a separate entry from the X-type site on purpose: _resolve_occupation_state_placeholder distinguishes occupation states by exactly the pair (occupiedBy, boundTo), so merging the two site types would make cat-RDEt and catX-RDEt indistinguishable. A site is recorded as a chemical entity because cpo:boundTo and cpo:occupiedBy have chebi:ChemicalEntity as their range. No CAS/SMILES/InChI exists for a surface site. Two things keep this entry out of the way when a real species is being looked up: callers that want a species pass NON_SPECIES_TYPES to ask_chemical_entity, which filters cpo:ActiveSite out of search and creation, and _search_chemical_entities gives exact name matches precedence over substring matches - so a Name search for \"Platinum\" returns the metal alone, not everything containing that word."
    },
    {
      "@id": "chem:ActiveSite_0002",
      "@type": [
        "chebi:ChemicalEntity",
        "cpo:ActiveSite",
        "hlo:Fixed"
      ],
      "schema:name": "Platinum active site (X-type)",
      "dcterms:isPartOf": {
        "@id": "chem:Molecule_0002"
      },
      "schema:comment": "A second, distinguishable kind of site on the platinum catalyst surface (dcterms:isPartOf chem:Molecule_0002) - it binds an RDEt molecule, which then becomes reactive towards RYE and REA (the two dimerisations). Carrier of cpo:boundTo on the occupation states cat(X) and catX-RDEt; the reaction library placeholder placeholder:CatalystSiteX resolves to this entry. See chem:ActiveSite_0001 for why the two site types are separate entries."
    },
    {
      "@id": "chem:ChemicalEntity_0001",
      "@type": [
        "chebi:ChemicalEntity",
        "hlo:Fixed"
      ],
      "schema:name": "Glass",
      "cpo:isInert": true,
      "rdfs:comment": "Informal entry, not a single chemical species - glass is an amorphous mixture. Kept as a chemical entity because cpo:madeOfMaterial resolves through a material to its phases, and a phase lists its constituents as chebi:ChemicalEntity. No CAS/SMILES/InChI/molar mass exists for it, which is why it carries neither - unlike every chebi:Molecule in this library. Moved here from device_library.jsonld on 2026-09-22, where it used to sit under the foreign chebi: namespace."
    },
    {
      "@id": "chem:ChemicalEntity_0002",
      "@type": [
        "chebi:ChemicalEntity",
        "hlo:Fixed"
      ],
      "schema:name": "Stainless steel",
      "cpo:isInert": true,
      "rdfs:comment": "Informal entry, not a single chemical species - stainless steel is an alloy. Same reasoning as chem:ChemicalEntity_0001 (Glass): carried as a chemical entity so a device body phase can list what it is made of, without CAS/SMILES/InChI/molar mass. Moved here from device_library.jsonld on 2026-09-22."
    },
    {
      "@id": "chem:ChemicalEntity_0003",
      "@type": [
        "chebi:ChemicalEntity",
        "hlo:Fixed"
      ],
      "schema:name": "Polypropylene",
      "cpo:isInert": true,
      "rdfs:comment": "Informal entry, not a single chemical species - polypropylene is a polymer with a distribution of chain lengths. Same reasoning as chem:ChemicalEntity_0001 (Glass) and _0002 (Stainless steel): carried as a chemical entity so a device body phase can list what it is made of, without CAS/SMILES/InChI/molar mass. Added 2026-09-22 for device:syringe_template."
    },
    {
      "@id": "chem:ChemicalEntity_0004",
      "@type": [
        "chebi:ChemicalEntity",
        "hlo:Fixed"
      ],
      "schema:name": "PTFE",
      "cpo:isInert": true,
      "rdfs:comment": "Informal entry, not a single chemical species - polytetrafluoroethylene is a polymer. Same reasoning as chem:ChemicalEntity_0001 (Glass): carried as a chemical entity so a device body phase can list what it is made of, without CAS/SMILES/InChI/molar mass. Added 2026-09-26 for device:vial_septum_template (the sample side of the septum)."
    },
