      ],
      "schema:name": "Fused quartz",
      "cpo:isInert": true,
      "rdfs:comment": "Informal entry, not a single chemical species - fused quartz is amorphous silicon dioxide, a glass. Same reasoning as chem:ChemicalEntity_0001 (Glass): carried as a chemical entity so a device body phase can list what it is made of, without CAS/SMILES/InChI/molar mass. Added 2026-10-05 for the capillaries of the K1 reactor.",
      "schema:comment": "Added by curation; not in the ELN (Patent US11724241B2, 'Constant shear continuous reactor device' (N. Jose, A. Lapkin; Cambridge Enterprise), example annular microreactor; patents.google.com/patent/US11724241B2) - suggested by Claude Code, confirmed by Laura Fadler on 05.10.2026 for the series pba_synthesis."
    },
