      "schema:comment": "PBA product of nickel(II) chloride and manganese(II) nitrate with potassium ferrocyanide, NiMn[Fe(CN)6]. Idealized composition: no potassium, water or vacancies in the lattice, and the two metals equimolar, as planned (Ni:Mn = 1:1, Laura Fadler and Meng Kong, 07.10.2026) - the real composition of the precipitate is only known after its characterization (Laura Fadler, 05.10.2026). Added by curation for the PBA series pba_synthesis (suggested by Claude Code, confirmed by Laura Fadler on 05.10.2026 for the series pba_synthesis); not on PubChem (looked up by the SMILES [C-]#N.[C-]#N.[C-]#N.[C-]#N.[C-]#N.[C-]#N.[Fe+2].[Ni+2].[Mn+2]), so no CAS, InChI or CID; formula and SMILES written by curation. Manganese(II) nitrate instead of the chloride since 08.10.2026 (projects/pba_synthesis/curation/archive/switch_pba_manganese_to_nitrate.py): the salt of 10 April 2026 is not recorded, the only one the files name is Mn(NO3)2 (run log of 12.03.2026); the tetrahydrate is assumed - Laura Fadler and Meng Kong, 08.10.2026.",
      "cpo:hasMolarMass": {
        "@id": "chem:NickelManganeseHexacyanoferrateII_MolarMass"
      }
    },
